# Counts events per type in a window, counting each `event_id` ONCE.
#
# `FINAL` is what makes that true. ReplacingMergeTree collapses duplicates when parts merge,
# and merges happen on their own schedule — so a plain `count()` over the raw table returns a
# number that drifts downward as background merges catch up. `FINAL` resolves the duplicates at
# read time instead, which is why an at-least-once source needs it and an exactly-once source
# would not.
#
# The cost is real: `FINAL` reads and merges at query time. For dashboards over a bounded window
# it is the right trade; for high-cardinality scans it is not, and `tinybird/README.md` records
# the upgrade path.

TOKEN "events_read" READ

NODE counts
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        event_type,
        count() AS events
    FROM events FINAL
    WHERE occurred_at >= {{DateTime64(start, '2000-01-01 00:00:00.000')}}
      AND occurred_at < {{DateTime64(end, '2100-01-01 00:00:00.000')}}
    GROUP BY event_type
    ORDER BY events DESC
    LIMIT {{Int32(limit, 100)}}

TYPE endpoint
